> Time: 1453733826 / Mon, 25 Jan 2016 14:57:06 +0000
> URL: /index.php?/REST/Forums/topic?startFromPostId=1909904&SessionId=386e017925c94a5c62631c4ade5f8688
> User JodieLawrence (286032)
Request Time: 1 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":{"State":"open","OpenTime":0,"CloseTime":0,"IsApproved":true,"IsPinned":false,"IsDeleted":false,"IsHidden":false,"IsArchived":false,"IsFollowing":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanReply":false,"CanFollow":true,"TotalPosts":3,"QueuedPosts":0,"DeletedPosts":0,"HasUnreadPosts":true,"HasAttachments":false,"Views":109,"MovedTo":null,"MovedOn":0,"FirstPostId":1909904,"Rating":0,"RatingHits":0,"Starter":{"Id":286002,"Name":"savanaray","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-286002.jpg?_r=1453488496","PhotoWidth":60,"PhotoHeight":80,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"StartDate":1453489651,"LastPoster":{"Id":283718,"Name":"SparkyM","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-283718.png?_r=1446004687","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":152,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"PollState":"0","LastVote":0,"ForumId":14,"Preview":{"Id":1909904,"PostDate":1453489651,"PostContent":"Hi everyone!   So I got engaged in December and right away I started planning, even though our we...","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"savanaray@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"76.25.39.119","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1453488492,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-286002.jpg?_r=1453488496","PhotoWidth":60,"PhotoHeight":80,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"savanaray","Id":286002,"Name":"savanaray","IsOnline":false}},"Posts":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"76.25.39.119","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79886,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"a3fb997dff4bb9908c34cd7c9c216613","RawContent":"Hi everyone! \n\n So I got engaged in December and right away I started planning, even though our wedding isn&#039;t till July 2017. Of course I already had a Pinterest board from before I was even dating my fianc\u00e9 so I already had an idea of what I wanted. Oregon is what I want. I love it so much. We went to Portland for vacation last February and I was ready to move there. My fianc\u00e9 loves it too, and we both would love to live there someday. Anyways...I found the perfect venue and we both instantly agreed on it. He emailed the venue and got prices and more pictures. It was all perfect...until my fianc\u00e9 suddenly changed his mind. \n\n\nWe live in Denver and both of our immediate families live here as well, and of course most of our friends. So when my fianc\u00e9 started thinking about everyone else having to travel for our wedding he suddenly was against the idea. Honestly a wedding in Colorado is going to be very expensive because we both want a mountain setting with trees, but all the venues like that are in ski towns. Which means the venues are very expensive and so is lodging for our guests. But if we had a wedding in Oregon we&#039;re asking our guests to buy a plane ticket, a hotel room and probably a rental car since my venue is on the coast, about 2 hours from the airport. \n\n\nI defiantly see my fianc\u00e9s point, he doesn&#039;t want to inconvenience anyone. But at the same time, I have my heart set on this venue in Oregon. I want my family and friends to see why I love Oregon and I want them to experience it. I want my wedding to be unique and memorable. I know it isn&#039;t a trip to Mexico or Hawaii, but it&#039;s still a mini vacation for everyone! \n\n\nWhenever we try to sit down and talk about what to do I get knots in my stomach because I know we aren&#039;t going to agree. He is thinking of everyone else and I&#039;m being selfish and thinking about what we want. But if someone can&#039;t come, that&#039;s fine! I won&#039;t be mad! I won&#039;t hold it against anyone. But is it wrong for me to even ask people to travel out of state for my wedding? Especially since it&#039;s just because I love the state and the scenery? Is that not a good enough reason to get married somewhere? How much is too much to expect your guests to spend when traveling for your wedding? \n\n\nSorry this is so long! I could definitely keep rambling but I&#039;ll leave it at this for now!   \n\n\nThank you!! \n\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1909904,"PostDate":1453489651,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Hi everyone! <br>\n So I got engaged in December and right away I started planning, even though our wedding isn't till July 2017. Of course I already had a Pinterest board from before I was even dating my fianc\u00e9 so I already had an idea of what I wanted. Oregon is what I want. I love it so much. We went to Portland for vacation last February and I was ready to move there. My fianc\u00e9 loves it too, and we both would love to live there someday. Anyways...I found the perfect venue and we both instantly agreed on it. He emailed the venue and got prices and more pictures. It was all perfect...until my fianc\u00e9 suddenly changed his mind. <br><br>\nWe live in Denver and both of our immediate families live here as well, and of course most of our friends. So when my fianc\u00e9 started thinking about everyone else having to travel for our wedding he suddenly was against the idea. Honestly a wedding in Colorado is going to be very expensive because we both want a mountain setting with trees, but all the venues like that are in ski towns. Which means the venues are very expensive and so is lodging for our guests. But if we had a wedding in Oregon we're asking our guests to buy a plane ticket, a hotel room and probably a rental car since my venue is on the coast, about 2 hours from the airport. <br><br>\nI defiantly see my fianc\u00e9s point, he doesn't want to inconvenience anyone. But at the same time, I have my heart set on this venue in Oregon. I want my family and friends to see why I love Oregon and I want them to experience it. I want my wedding to be unique and memorable. I know it isn't a trip to Mexico or Hawaii, but it's still a mini vacation for everyone! <br><br>\nWhenever we try to sit down and talk about what to do I get knots in my stomach because I know we aren't going to agree. He is thinking of everyone else and I'm being selfish and thinking about what we want. But if someone can't come, that's fine! I won't be mad! I won't hold it against anyone. But is it wrong for me to even ask people to travel out of state for my wedding? Especially since it's just because I love the state and the scenery? Is that not a good enough reason to get married somewhere? How much is too much to expect your guests to spend when traveling for your wedding? <br><br>\nSorry this is so long! I could definitely keep rambling but I'll leave it at this for now!   <br><br>\nThank you!! <br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"savanaray@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"76.25.39.119","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1453488492,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-286002.jpg?_r=1453488496","PhotoWidth":60,"PhotoHeight":80,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"savanaray","Id":286002,"Name":"savanaray","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"142.161.170.48","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79886,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"797fe792af85d364df4c4584c8f15f9a","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Congrats on your engagement and upcoming wedding next July, savanaray!!! You&#039;ll find lots of great ideas, suggestions and support from everyone at these boards, so you&#039;re already off to a wonderful start here :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We&#039;ve found every wedding is as unique and varied as each couple is, so there are limitless possibilities! One key is to find what works for YOU guys...that&#039;s what will lead to your best decisions.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;You&#039;re planning a whole life together, so this could be a wonderful starting point in working out solutions that work for you both, and finding compromises that serve both of you :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Wishing you happy research, and that it all works out for the BEST!!! cheers - team MTM :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"https:\/\/scontent-yyz1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xaf1\/t31.0-8\/1557351_10152516887594487_6618319857352960386_o.jpg\" alt=\"1557351_10152516887594487_66183198573529\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"https:\/\/scontent-yyz1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xft1\/t31.0-8\/11427375_10153408854794487_4566310682341134022_o.jpg\" alt=\"11427375_10153408854794487_4566310682341\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"https:\/\/scontent-yyz1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xfa1\/t31.0-8\/11259186_10153293779444487_2885543162038044747_o.jpg\" alt=\"11259186_10153293779444487_2885543162038\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1909905,"PostDate":1453491141,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Congrats on your engagement and upcoming wedding next July, savanaray!!! You'll find lots of great ideas, suggestions and support from everyone at these boards, so you're already off to a wonderful start here <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We've found every wedding is as unique and varied as each couple is, so there are limitless possibilities! One key is to find what works for YOU guys...that's what will lead to your best decisions.<\/p>\n<p>You're planning a whole life together, so this could be a wonderful starting point in working out solutions that work for you both, and finding compromises that serve both of you <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wishing you happy research, and that it all works out for the BEST!!! cheers - team MTM <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/scontent-yyz1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xaf1\/t31.0-8\/1557351_10152516887594487_6618319857352960386_o.jpg\" alt=\"1557351_10152516887594487_66183198573529\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/scontent-yyz1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xft1\/t31.0-8\/11427375_10153408854794487_4566310682341134022_o.jpg\" alt=\"11427375_10153408854794487_4566310682341\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/scontent-yyz1-1.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xfa1\/t31.0-8\/11259186_10153293779444487_2885543162038044747_o.jpg\" alt=\"11259186_10153293779444487_2885543162038\"><\/span><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p><img src=\"http:\/\/i711.photobucket.com\/albums\/ww116\/momentsthatmatter\/MTMLogo08-1.png\" alt=\"MTMLogo08-1.png\"><\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.momentsthatmatterphotography.com'><strong><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Moments That Matter Photography Studios, Playa del Carmen, Mexico<\/span><\/strong><\/a><\/p>\n<p>Canadian Award Winning Photojournalist serving Mayan Riviera<br>\nEmail: <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='mailto:contact@momentsthatmatterphotography.com'>contact@momentsthatmatterphotography.com<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Scoop on what we do:\u00a0 <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/reviews\/r\/4212-beautiful-november-wedding\/#review'>MTM Reviews<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Meet Lincoln & Team MTM: <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/vimeo.com\/51032621'>\"Meet Lincoln\" Video + see his Passion!!!<\/a>","Email":"momentsthatmatterphotography@gmail.com","IpAddress":"189.221.252.187","GroupId":49,"GroupName":"Insiders","JoinDate":1280210660,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-230711.png?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Moments That Matter","Id":230711,"Name":"Moments That Matter","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"99.67.60.56","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79886,"EditedBy":"<strong>Edited by SparkyM, 23 January 2016 - 01:55 AM.<\/strong>","EditDate":1453542929,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"5b20dd19e58f8eb79722111c1dc02eb3","RawContent":"Welcome Savanaray!  Sorry to hear you&#039;re in a pickle with choosing the best venue for the wedding.  I second everything that Moments that Matter said, and would add one tiny reminder. It&#039;s YOUR Wedding!!! Everyone is going to have an opinion about it all.  The important thing is that you do what your heart wants and the people who really matter will figure out a way to be there!  Plus you&#039;re giving them plenty of time to save, plan and budget for it!  Good luck &amp;amp; all the best!  Happy collaborating and planning \ud83d\ude0a\nAlso I&#039;m originally from Breckenridge.  If you do end up having it in Colorado, Check out the amphitheater in Dillon (right on the lake... gorgeous!!) or the top of Swan Mountain road.  A beautiful pathway that goes and overlooks the lake &amp;amp; 10mile range.  Food for thought :-)\nLast thought: May, end of May and the beginning of June are far less busy in resort towns.  You may look at moving your date to then to save some $$$ and get more bang for your buck :-)","Attachments":[],"Id":1909916,"PostDate":1453543369,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Welcome Savanaray!  Sorry to hear you're in a pickle with choosing the best venue for the wedding.  I second everything that Moments that Matter said, and would add one tiny reminder. It's YOUR Wedding!!! Everyone is going to have an opinion about it all.  The important thing is that you do what your heart wants and the people who really matter will figure out a way to be there!  Plus you're giving them plenty of time to save, plan and budget for it!  Good luck & all the best!  Happy collaborating and planning \ud83d\ude0a<br \/>Also I'm originally from Breckenridge.  If you do end up having it in Colorado, Check out the amphitheater in Dillon (right on the lake... gorgeous!!) or the top of Swan Mountain road.  A beautiful pathway that goes and overlooks the lake & 10mile range.  Food for thought :-)<br \/>Last thought: May, end of May and the beginning of June are far less busy in resort towns.  You may look at moving your date to then to save some $$$ and get more bang for your buck :-)\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"jeffandshauna2015@gmail.com","IpAddress":"99.67.60.33","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1435400211,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-283718.png?_r=1446004687","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":152,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"SparkyM","Id":283718,"Name":"SparkyM","IsOnline":false}}],"Id":"79886","Title":"Destination Wedding In Oregon","LastPostDate":1453543369},"Pages":{"TotalItems":3,"TotalPages":1,"CurrentPage":0,"NextPage":-1,"PreviousPage":-1,"LastPage":0},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
